WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:03.269
-Texas and Mississippi announced

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:04.837
that they're lifting
their COVID restrictions,

00:00:04.837 --> 00:00:07.873
including mask mandates
against the strong warnings

00:00:07.873 --> 00:00:10.643
of public health officials,
and the same Republicans,

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:12.912
putting workers in harm's way
are also silent

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:16.048
on a courageous drive
to unionize Amazon workers.

00:00:16.048 --> 00:00:18.217
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:18.217 --> 00:00:22.121
♪♪

00:00:22.121 --> 00:00:25.224
We are tantalizingly close
to what could very well

00:00:25.224 --> 00:00:26.759
be the end of
the COVID pandemic.

00:00:26.759 --> 00:00:29.061
No one knows exactly
when that could happen.

00:00:29.061 --> 00:00:31.297
Predictions for when
we'll hit herd immunity

00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:33.499
and return to normal range
from as early as April

00:00:33.499 --> 00:00:34.600
to as late as Christmas.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:36.368
But we know with vaccines

00:00:36.368 --> 00:00:38.137
ramping up
and cases trending down,

00:00:38.137 --> 00:00:40.240
especially as we get
closer to summer,

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:42.142
there are genuine reasons
for optimism.

00:00:42.142 --> 00:00:43.342
And I know it's hard to believe.

00:00:43.342 --> 00:00:45.044
When I hear good news,
it's like when a vegan

00:00:45.044 --> 00:00:46.613
eats a cheeseburger.

00:00:46.613 --> 00:00:49.082
My body
doesn't know what to do with it,

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:50.950
but it knows it's good.

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:54.053
Our souls have all been ground
to dust by a relentless winter

00:00:54.053 --> 00:00:55.655
and a year
of being trapped indoors,

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:57.624
drinking gin straight
from the bottle

00:00:57.624 --> 00:01:00.526
and bingeing increasingly
obscure TV shows.

00:01:00.526 --> 00:01:03.129
It got so bad I downloaded
a German streaming service

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:05.131
called
<i> Unterhaltun fur die Menschen</i>

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:07.900
to watch a crime show that takes
place in Baden-Wuerttemberg,

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:10.670
starring famed German character
actor Albert Van Mueller-Schmidt

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:12.771
as Detective Otto Jaegerhauer.

00:01:12.771 --> 00:01:14.307
Oh, man, let me tell you,

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:17.577
episode three
is a real "clippenbugel."

00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:20.613
That's German for cliffhanger.

00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:22.448
Anyway, the point
is we're so close,

00:01:22.448 --> 00:01:23.883
we can't screw it up now.

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:25.151
We need to spend the next two

00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:26.819
or three months
really crushing this thing

00:01:26.819 --> 00:01:29.188
so we can all have
a potentially beautiful summer.

00:01:29.188 --> 00:01:32.224
The Senate is on the verge
of passing a massive COVID

00:01:32.224 --> 00:01:34.626
relief plan to help get everyone
through the next few months.

00:01:34.626 --> 00:01:36.829
And President Biden
has announced a production deal

00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:37.964
that could ensure vaccines

00:01:37.964 --> 00:01:39.198
for every American
by the end of May.

00:01:39.198 --> 00:01:40.332
Think about that.

00:01:40.332 --> 00:01:42.535
Come July 4th,
you could be knocking back

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:44.003
a cold one
in your neighbor's yard

00:01:44.003 --> 00:01:45.938
while he flips burgers
and drones on

00:01:45.938 --> 00:01:48.074
about how much better
it is to cook with charcoal.

00:01:48.074 --> 00:01:50.310
You'll be seeing
so much of your neighbors,

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:53.012
you'll start praying
for the next pandemic.

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:54.614
We could get there.
It's possible.

00:01:54.614 --> 00:01:56.448
We just have to spend the next
few months not screwing up,

00:01:56.448 --> 00:01:58.550
which of course,
means some governors immediately

00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:00.219
started racing
to screw it up.

00:02:00.219 --> 00:02:02.721
-The governors of Texas
and Mississippi say

00:02:02.721 --> 00:02:05.891
they are lifting nearly all of
their states' coronavirus

00:02:05.891 --> 00:02:09.295
restrictions and mask mandates
in the coming days,

00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:11.598
now despite new warnings
that the US could soon face

00:02:11.598 --> 00:02:14.200
a deadly fourth surge
of the virus.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.603
-Health officials
are warning Americans

00:02:16.603 --> 00:02:18.737
should not become complacent

00:02:18.737 --> 00:02:20.973
because this pandemic
is not over yet.

00:02:20.973 --> 00:02:24.377
We are still seeing roughly
1,500 deaths

00:02:24.377 --> 00:02:26.111
every single day
from the virus.

00:02:26.111 --> 00:02:30.516
-All businesses of any type
are allowed

00:02:30.516 --> 00:02:33.286
to open 100%.

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:38.624
Also, I am ending
the statewide mask mandate.

00:02:38.624 --> 00:02:42.662
-Your reaction to the governor's
announcement today?

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:46.199
-Insanity. I'd like to say that
Governor Abbott

00:02:46.199 --> 00:02:47.766
has lost his mind.

00:02:47.766 --> 00:02:49.502
-In fairness,
maybe he didn't lose it.

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:51.905
Maybe it just froze during
the massive power failure

00:02:51.905 --> 00:02:53.372
that happened on his watch.

00:02:53.372 --> 00:02:55.607
-Damn it, guys, we're so close.
Why are you doing this now?

00:02:55.607 --> 00:02:58.578
You really want people
to congregate at full capacity

00:02:58.578 --> 00:03:00.079
in bars and gyms and nightclubs?

00:03:00.079 --> 00:03:01.280
I wouldn't even go to a

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:02.982
full capacity nightclub
without a pandemic.

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:03.850
I mean, why?

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:05.717
So I can awkwardly wave my hands

00:03:05.717 --> 00:03:06.919
in the air to some EDM

00:03:06.919 --> 00:03:08.988
while a jacked due on molly
touches my face

00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:10.589
and asks me how Stefon is?

00:03:10.589 --> 00:03:11.958
He's fine.

00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:14.827
He's fine and he's fictional.

00:03:14.827 --> 00:03:16.896
And by the way,
this isn't the fault of Texans.

00:03:16.896 --> 00:03:20.533
They need and deserve help and
vaccines as much as anyone else.

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:22.201
It's the fault
of their political leaders.

00:03:22.201 --> 00:03:23.302
And look, I get it.

00:03:23.302 --> 00:03:25.037
Businesses really
are struggling.

00:03:25.037 --> 00:03:27.139
It's still too early
to reopen the riskiest ones,

00:03:27.139 --> 00:03:29.208
and we should just be giving
everyone money to survive.

00:03:29.208 --> 00:03:31.410
But I understand --
it's a difficult trade off.

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:33.612
But rescinding
the mask mandates?

00:03:33.612 --> 00:03:35.047
That's just full insanity.

00:03:35.047 --> 00:03:36.949
Masks work.
There's so much proof.

00:03:36.949 --> 00:03:38.517
Thanks to masks and
social distancing,

00:03:38.517 --> 00:03:40.820
the flu basically
vanished this year.

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:43.355
Meanwhile, South Dakota resisted
a mask mandate

00:03:43.355 --> 00:03:44.756
and that state's mortality rate

00:03:44.756 --> 00:03:46.959
has been the highest
in the country since last July.

00:03:46.959 --> 00:03:50.529
Masks can actually help us
open up more safely.

00:03:50.529 --> 00:03:52.398
Plus, I got to be honest,
I'm surprised politicians

00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:55.401
that are so pro cowboy hat
find masks uncomfortable.

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:58.937
Maybe it's my weak neck, but I'd
rather wear 100 masks

00:03:58.937 --> 00:04:00.540
than one of those big ol' hats.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:03.342
That's a shame though, because
I look very good and natural

00:04:03.342 --> 00:04:05.611
when I wear one.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.611 --> 00:04:07.446
That's real.
That's not Photoshop.

00:04:07.446 --> 00:04:09.148
One of the most galling parts

00:04:09.148 --> 00:04:11.383
of rescinding the mask mandates
is that many of the people

00:04:11.383 --> 00:04:13.085
who will suffer
most are workers.

00:04:13.085 --> 00:04:14.887
The mask isn't just
for your safety,

00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:17.757
it's for the safety
of those around you.

00:04:17.757 --> 00:04:20.692
Workers who have no choice
but to show up to their jobs

00:04:20.692 --> 00:04:21.927
in person will be at risk

00:04:21.927 --> 00:04:23.262
and the politicians
will be fine.

00:04:23.262 --> 00:04:25.031
So, please, keep wearing a mask.

00:04:25.031 --> 00:04:26.766
The last thing
a Footlocker employee needs

00:04:26.766 --> 00:04:28.201
is for you to show up maskless

00:04:28.201 --> 00:04:30.602
and spend an hour trying on
different sizes of red Yeezys

00:04:30.602 --> 00:04:32.471
that are gonna look ridiculous
on you no matter what.

00:04:32.471 --> 00:04:34.240
And by the way,
this is the same party

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:35.775
that, as we speak,

00:04:35.775 --> 00:04:38.477
is trying to rebrand itself
as a workers' party,

00:04:38.477 --> 00:04:41.380
even as they needlessly
put workers in harms way.

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:43.082
In the aftermath
of the Trump presidency,

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:44.850
you've probably heard
a few Republicans

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:46.819
ludicrously trying
to rebrand themselves

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:49.088
as the champions
of the working class.

00:04:49.088 --> 00:04:50.423
You know, the same guys who cram

00:04:50.423 --> 00:04:53.092
through a $2 trillion tax cut

00:04:53.092 --> 00:04:55.694
for corporations and the wealthy
in the dead of night

00:04:55.694 --> 00:04:58.197
without a single hearing
and literally scribbled notes

00:04:58.197 --> 00:04:59.865
in the margins
at the last minute

00:04:59.865 --> 00:05:01.133
to make it easier
for the wealthy

00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:03.435
to avoid taxes by using
pass-through companies.

00:05:03.435 --> 00:05:06.272
All that stuff Springsteen's
always singing about.

00:05:06.272 --> 00:05:09.142
♪ Got a wife and kids
in Baltimore, Jack ♪

00:05:09.142 --> 00:05:11.143
♪ But I can claim them
as consultants ♪

00:05:11.143 --> 00:05:14.180
♪ And I get it all back ♪
[ Laughter ]

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:16.148
I mean, now it's good.
I had a bad one last week,

00:05:16.148 --> 00:05:18.184
but now it's fully
like he's here.

00:05:18.184 --> 00:05:20.285
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.285 --> 00:05:21.787
Remember when Elizabeth Warren,

00:05:21.787 --> 00:05:24.523
who is now pushing for a wealth
tax on the richest Americans,

00:05:24.523 --> 00:05:26.658
that the fake Republican
populists also opposed,

00:05:26.658 --> 00:05:28.894
tried to read the text
of the GOP tax cut

00:05:28.894 --> 00:05:30.763
and couldn't even make out
what it said?

00:05:30.763 --> 00:05:35.168
-They're sending around
their edits as we speak.

00:05:35.168 --> 00:05:39.238
"Adjustments attributable to
conversion from S corporat--"

00:05:39.238 --> 00:05:43.776
Oh, it's been cut off --
"to corporation.

00:05:43.776 --> 00:05:48.780
Section 481 is amended
by adding at the N."

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:50.349
I assume they mean "end,"

00:05:50.349 --> 00:05:51.884
but again, it's all cut off.

00:05:51.884 --> 00:05:55.221
"The following new subsection,
adjustments

00:05:55.221 --> 00:06:01.426
attributable to conversion
for a corporation..."

00:06:01.426 --> 00:06:03.996
Something.
C Corporation.

00:06:03.996 --> 00:06:06.832
Per in...

00:06:06.832 --> 00:06:09.401
Dangerous? That can't be right.

00:06:09.401 --> 00:06:11.170
-Sounds like she's trying
to read the text

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:13.038
on a bottle
of Dr. Bronner's.

00:06:13.038 --> 00:06:16.909
Made with mint, lavender,
juniper, and...

00:06:16.909 --> 00:06:18.310
whale meat?

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:20.012
That can't be right.

00:06:20.012 --> 00:06:21.180
By the time they were
done with it,

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:22.781
that bill looked like
a science textbook

00:06:22.781 --> 00:06:25.184
you got for six dollars
at an off-campus bookstore,

00:06:25.184 --> 00:06:27.954
the one where the last paragraph
says, "As of this publishing,

00:06:27.954 --> 00:06:30.889
Jonas Salk is getting
some promising results."

00:06:30.889 --> 00:06:32.358
And I have to say,
watching a Harvard professor

00:06:32.358 --> 00:06:35.093
try to make heads or tails
of nonsensical writing

00:06:35.093 --> 00:06:37.396
gave me chilling flashbacks
to college.

00:06:37.396 --> 00:06:40.766
"So that's why Pacino
and De Niro make convincing,

00:06:40.766 --> 00:06:44.337
if unlikely, adversaries
in the movie 'Heat.'

00:06:44.337 --> 00:06:45.838
Now, Mr. Meyers, you do know

00:06:45.838 --> 00:06:47.540
this is a chemistry class,
right?"

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:49.374
"Hey, you're not going
to find better chemistry

00:06:49.374 --> 00:06:51.143
than De Niro and Pacino
in their prime.

00:06:51.143 --> 00:06:53.412
That is a much
more explosive combo

00:06:53.412 --> 00:06:55.481
than hydrogen peroxide
and sodium iodide."

00:06:55.481 --> 00:06:56.649
[ Chuckles ]

00:06:56.649 --> 00:06:59.551
They should do a remake
of that movie now.

00:06:59.551 --> 00:07:01.621
And instead of a diner,
they'd meet virtually.

00:07:01.621 --> 00:07:04.824
"Thanks for meeting me
in the Zoom room!

00:07:04.824 --> 00:07:08.527
All ready to Zoom tonight,
baby!"

00:07:08.527 --> 00:07:11.964
"I can't hear you. Somebody
muted you. Somebody muted you."

00:07:11.964 --> 00:07:15.267
"What? I'm on mute?

00:07:15.267 --> 00:07:21.174
Nobody mutes
Alfredo James Pacino!

00:07:21.174 --> 00:07:24.577
My mic is always hot, baby!

00:07:24.577 --> 00:07:26.311
[ Laughter ]

00:07:26.311 --> 00:07:29.582
And I'm feeling sky-high!"

00:07:34.453 --> 00:07:38.891
It's very nice when there are
no people here...

00:07:38.891 --> 00:07:40.793
'cause then I can give
the people what they want.

00:07:40.793 --> 00:07:43.762
[ Laughter ]

00:07:43.762 --> 00:07:46.232
So, the same guys who wrote
and voted

00:07:46.232 --> 00:07:48.867
for that massive giveaway
to corporations and the wealthy

00:07:48.867 --> 00:07:51.103
who are needlessly
putting workers in harms way

00:07:51.103 --> 00:07:52.638
by repealing mask mandates

00:07:52.638 --> 00:07:55.007
and using them as cannon
fodder against the virus

00:07:55.007 --> 00:07:57.143
are now trying
to rebrand themselves

00:07:57.143 --> 00:07:58.844
as working class populists.

00:07:58.844 --> 00:08:00.980
Texas Senator Ted Cruz
tried that last week

00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:02.982
at the Conservative
Political Action Conference

00:08:02.982 --> 00:08:05.251
and then again this week
on Fox News.

00:08:05.251 --> 00:08:07.753
-The Democratic Party
has abandoned

00:08:07.753 --> 00:08:09.188
the working class men and women,

00:08:09.188 --> 00:08:11.023
the millions of people
who are out of jobs,

00:08:11.023 --> 00:08:13.258
who are seeing their wages
pulled down,

00:08:13.258 --> 00:08:15.661
who are competing to provide
for their families

00:08:15.661 --> 00:08:17.996
with people coming illegally.

00:08:17.996 --> 00:08:20.299
That's not who the Democratic
Party represents anymore.

00:08:20.299 --> 00:08:21.800
They don't represent
unions anymore.

00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:23.669
They don't represent
construction workers

00:08:23.669 --> 00:08:25.070
or truck drivers

00:08:25.070 --> 00:08:26.772
or working men
and women anymore.

00:08:26.772 --> 00:08:29.909
The Republican Party

00:08:29.909 --> 00:08:32.611
is not the party
just of the country clubs.

00:08:32.611 --> 00:08:35.981
The Republican Party
is the party of steelworkers

00:08:35.981 --> 00:08:37.549
and construction workers

00:08:37.549 --> 00:08:41.253
and pipeline workers
and taxi cab drivers

00:08:41.253 --> 00:08:45.190
and cops and firefighters
and waiters and waitresses

00:08:45.190 --> 00:08:47.559
and the men and women
with calluses on their hands

00:08:47.559 --> 00:08:49.428
who are working
for this country.

00:08:49.428 --> 00:08:50.930
That is our party!

00:08:50.930 --> 00:08:53.031
Oh, please, Ted Cruz,
your hands are so delicate

00:08:53.031 --> 00:08:55.768
you need an epidural
to get through a manicure.

00:08:55.768 --> 00:08:57.837
The only calluses Ted Cruz
has on his hands

00:08:57.837 --> 00:08:59.838
or for checking Kayak
on his phone.

00:08:59.838 --> 00:09:02.040
Also, I'm willing to bet
the only truck driver Cruz

00:09:02.040 --> 00:09:03.709
has ever met is this guy.

00:09:03.709 --> 00:09:05.811
But yeah, sure, we all believe
you're a pro-union,

00:09:05.811 --> 00:09:08.114
blue-collar guy who's fighting
for working people

00:09:08.114 --> 00:09:10.816
from your flight
to the Ritz-Carlton in Cancun.

00:09:10.816 --> 00:09:12.384
I'm sure
those construction workers

00:09:12.384 --> 00:09:14.086
you're pretending to care
about are thrilled

00:09:14.086 --> 00:09:16.088
that, thanks to the tax bill
you voted for,

00:09:16.088 --> 00:09:19.524
they can finally convert their
S corporations to C corporations

00:09:19.524 --> 00:09:21.327
and use their corporate
pass-through vehicles

00:09:21.327 --> 00:09:22.762
to reduce their tax liability.

00:09:22.762 --> 00:09:25.864
Everybody remembers
the famous photo of steelworkers

00:09:25.864 --> 00:09:27.332
sitting atop a skyscraper.

00:09:27.332 --> 00:09:30.069
But did you know they wrote off
those lunchboxes

00:09:30.069 --> 00:09:32.204
as business expenses
by funneling their income

00:09:32.204 --> 00:09:33.939
through a limited
liability company?

00:09:33.939 --> 00:09:37.209
But if Ted Cruz and his fellow
faux-populist hucksters

00:09:37.209 --> 00:09:38.910
like Missouri Senator
Josh Hawley,

00:09:38.910 --> 00:09:40.913
really wanted to prove

00:09:40.913 --> 00:09:43.381
they're supposed pro-union
blue-collar bona fides,

00:09:43.381 --> 00:09:46.852
they could easily speak up
in favor of a courageous

00:09:46.852 --> 00:09:50.356
and unprecedented union drive
by Amazon workers in Alabama,

00:09:50.356 --> 00:09:53.292
because right now those workers
are bravely taking on

00:09:53.292 --> 00:09:55.695
one of the richest and most
powerful companies in the world.

00:09:55.695 --> 00:09:58.830
And the company is going to
extreme lengths to stop them.

00:09:58.830 --> 00:10:01.200
-An historic labor showdown
in Alabama tonight

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:03.969
involving the world's largest
online retailer,

00:10:03.969 --> 00:10:06.672
and it's drawing the attention
of the White House.

00:10:06.672 --> 00:10:09.107
Thousands of workers
at an Amazon warehouse

00:10:09.107 --> 00:10:10.375
voting on whether to form

00:10:10.375 --> 00:10:12.811
the company's first labor union
in the U.S.

00:10:12.811 --> 00:10:15.247
Amazon pushing employees
to vote no.

00:10:15.247 --> 00:10:18.951
-Bessemer, Alabama, is home
to an Amazon warehouse

00:10:18.951 --> 00:10:22.521
where about 6,000 employees
are voting right now

00:10:22.521 --> 00:10:26.891
on whether to form the Internet
giant's first union in the U.S.

00:10:26.891 --> 00:10:28.393
It's a bitter battle.

00:10:28.393 --> 00:10:31.130
Warehouse employees like
Jennifer Bates

00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:33.965
constantly get texts
from Amazon,

00:10:33.965 --> 00:10:36.468
warning that union
dues could leave them

00:10:36.468 --> 00:10:39.037
with less money
than they already have.

00:10:39.037 --> 00:10:41.740
Anti-union fliers
are even posted

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:44.810
inside a warehouse
bathroom stalls.

00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:47.513
-First of all, Amazon, stop
sending anti-union texts.

00:10:47.513 --> 00:10:49.581
In fact, stop sending
texts in general.

00:10:49.581 --> 00:10:51.083
Amazon texts me
more than my wife,

00:10:51.083 --> 00:10:54.253
especially when I ask her
about one of my impressions.

00:10:54.253 --> 00:10:56.155
Seriously, Amazon,
I don't need a text every time

00:10:56.155 --> 00:10:57.522
I place an order,
then another one

00:10:57.522 --> 00:10:59.058
when that order's received,
and then another

00:10:59.058 --> 00:11:00.225
when the package is shipped,

00:11:00.225 --> 00:11:01.460
and another
when it's dropped off.

00:11:01.460 --> 00:11:03.962
What's next --
a text when my neighbor gets mad

00:11:03.962 --> 00:11:06.498
that I left the package
in the hallway for too long

00:11:06.498 --> 00:11:08.067
and reports me
to the co-op board

00:11:08.067 --> 00:11:09.535
for a disciplinary hearing?

00:11:09.535 --> 00:11:12.204
Janet, I know you've been trying
to get me kicked out

00:11:12.204 --> 00:11:14.673
because you hate my welcome mat,
but too bad

00:11:14.673 --> 00:11:16.308
because I think it's funny...

00:11:16.308 --> 00:11:19.745
and we need to laugh, Janet!

00:11:19.745 --> 00:11:21.480
It's hard to overstate
just how seismic

00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:22.982
and historic
this union drive is.

00:11:22.982 --> 00:11:24.182
Amazon workers are fighting

00:11:24.182 --> 00:11:26.318
against the largest retailer
in the world

00:11:26.318 --> 00:11:27.953
run by one of the richest men
in the world,

00:11:27.953 --> 00:11:29.688
which is going all out
to stop them.

00:11:29.688 --> 00:11:32.892
-Why do you want to join a
union?

00:11:32.892 --> 00:11:36.661
-Because I feel like we need
an amplified voice.

00:11:36.661 --> 00:11:39.531
We've been talking to Amazon
about issues that we've had

00:11:39.531 --> 00:11:43.569
and they've ignored us,
so we need a sense of security

00:11:43.569 --> 00:11:47.572
and a louder voice
and better wages.

00:11:47.572 --> 00:11:50.442
-Amazon hired a group
of union buster consultants

00:11:50.442 --> 00:11:54.913
that they paid each consultant
$3,200 a day

00:11:54.913 --> 00:11:57.616
to try to convince these people
to vote against theirselves.

00:11:57.616 --> 00:12:01.386
Amazon is no more than when
we look at things down there,

00:12:01.386 --> 00:12:04.656
it's a sweat shop
and people are out there

00:12:04.656 --> 00:12:06.992
just working --
They have to touch a package.

00:12:06.992 --> 00:12:09.761
Every eight seconds
they have to touch a package.

00:12:09.761 --> 00:12:12.331
They're only allowed
two 30-minute break a day.

00:12:12.331 --> 00:12:14.533
-They have to touch a package
every eight seconds?

00:12:14.533 --> 00:12:15.901
That's insane.

00:12:15.901 --> 00:12:18.437
Not even
the TSA works that fast.

00:12:20.072 --> 00:12:22.674
[ Laughter ]

00:12:22.674 --> 00:12:24.410
Fred, where's my rimshot?

00:12:26.611 --> 00:12:31.183
Fred, that joke clearly called
for a rimshot, buddy.

00:12:31.183 --> 00:12:33.752
Okay, you know what? We're going
to have to have a meeting.

00:12:33.752 --> 00:12:35.454
Well, where was I?
Oh, right.

00:12:35.454 --> 00:12:37.923
They have to touch a package
every eight seconds.

00:12:37.923 --> 00:12:39.558
[ Rimshot ]

00:12:39.558 --> 00:12:42.060
[ Laughter ]

00:12:42.060 --> 00:12:45.263
Just too late, Fred.

00:12:45.263 --> 00:12:47.900
But also, it's insane they
only get two 30-minute breaks.

00:12:47.900 --> 00:12:49.801
They're essential workers
employed by a company

00:12:49.801 --> 00:12:51.236
whose CEO increased his wealth

00:12:51.236 --> 00:12:53.138
by $75 billion in 2020

00:12:53.138 --> 00:12:54.706
and they basically kept
the entire country

00:12:54.706 --> 00:12:55.874
running during a pandemic.

00:12:55.874 --> 00:12:57.509
Without Amazon, I probably

00:12:57.509 --> 00:13:00.012
would have had to camp out
at Trader Joe's for toilet paper

00:13:00.012 --> 00:13:03.448
like the standby line
for SNL when BTS performs

00:13:03.448 --> 00:13:04.983
or when I hosted.

00:13:04.983 --> 00:13:06.618
You should have seen the line.

00:13:06.618 --> 00:13:10.923
[ Wind howls ]

00:13:10.923 --> 00:13:14.893
I did not sign off
on adding a tumbleweed.

00:13:14.893 --> 00:13:17.863
[ Laughter ]

00:13:17.863 --> 00:13:19.932
This is an actual fight
by courageous

00:13:19.932 --> 00:13:23.001
working-class union organizers
against a corporate Goliath.

00:13:23.001 --> 00:13:25.336
If you were to actually take
the pretend populists

00:13:25.336 --> 00:13:26.805
of the GOP at their word,

00:13:26.805 --> 00:13:28.874
this is the exact kind of thing
they supposedly care about,

00:13:28.874 --> 00:13:30.408
and yet they've been silent.

00:13:30.408 --> 00:13:31.810
Meanwhile, Biden released
a major

00:13:31.810 --> 00:13:33.979
and truly unprecedented video
in support of the effort

00:13:33.979 --> 00:13:36.648
and without
mentioning Amazon by name,

00:13:36.648 --> 00:13:38.850
warned companies
to stop intimidating workers

00:13:38.850 --> 00:13:40.185
who want to unionize.

00:13:40.185 --> 00:13:44.723
-The choice to join a union
is up to the workers --

00:13:44.723 --> 00:13:46.825
full stop.

00:13:46.825 --> 00:13:48.394
Full stop.

00:13:48.394 --> 00:13:52.431
Today and over the next few days
and weeks, workers in Alabama

00:13:52.431 --> 00:13:54.099
and all across America
are voting

00:13:54.099 --> 00:13:57.969
on whether to organize
a union in their workplace.

00:13:57.969 --> 00:14:02.941
This is vitally important --
a vitally important choice.

00:14:02.941 --> 00:14:06.378
And there should be
no intimidation, no coercion,

00:14:06.378 --> 00:14:10.348
no threats,
no anti-union propaganda.

00:14:10.348 --> 00:14:13.885
No supervisor, no supervisors
should confront employees

00:14:13.885 --> 00:14:15.688
about their union preferences.

00:14:15.688 --> 00:14:17.289
-And of course
Joe came out for the union.

00:14:17.289 --> 00:14:19.691
He was one of those guys
eating lunch on that skyscraper.

00:14:19.691 --> 00:14:21.961
You think he's going
to be out-blue-collared

00:14:21.961 --> 00:14:23.362
by Ted Cruz, of all people?

00:14:23.362 --> 00:14:25.397
He's ridden Amtrak
so many times,

00:14:25.397 --> 00:14:27.633
he's probably got
a railroad union card.

00:14:27.633 --> 00:14:29.101
If politics didn't work out,

00:14:29.101 --> 00:14:32.203
his fallback plan was working
in the snack car on the Acela.

00:14:32.203 --> 00:14:36.475
"We got gum and coffee,
and that's it."

00:14:36.475 --> 00:14:39.077
So Biden came out forcefully
in favor of union rights.

00:14:39.077 --> 00:14:40.478
And yet we've heard
radio silence

00:14:40.478 --> 00:14:42.480
from the so-called populists
of the Republican Party

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:44.682
who pretend to be pro-worker
and anti-big tech,

00:14:44.682 --> 00:14:46.051
although in fairness,

00:14:46.051 --> 00:14:48.754
they do have much more important
things going on right now.

00:14:48.754 --> 00:14:50.555
-Well, first it was
Mr. Potato Head

00:14:50.555 --> 00:14:51.990
and Mrs. Potato Head,

00:14:51.990 --> 00:14:53.625
now it's Dr. Seuss.

00:14:53.625 --> 00:14:55.561
-They want to cancel
the Muppets.

00:14:55.561 --> 00:14:57.996
They want to cancel
Mr. and Mrs. Potato Head.

00:14:57.996 --> 00:14:59.664
So when will this stop?

00:14:59.664 --> 00:15:02.033
-You see last week they tried
to cancel Kermit the Frog

00:15:02.033 --> 00:15:03.835
and Mr. Potato Head?
You see that?

00:15:03.835 --> 00:15:06.638
-Look out, Mr. Potato Head.
You're next.

00:15:06.638 --> 00:15:08.640
-If I wanted to buy one
and let's say

00:15:08.640 --> 00:15:11.643
I had the boy at home
and I wanted the girl,

00:15:11.643 --> 00:15:14.079
the box is going to say
"potato head."

00:15:14.079 --> 00:15:16.081
How am I going to know
which one I'm getting?

00:15:16.081 --> 00:15:19.717
-This week alone, they canceled
Mr. Potato Head.

00:15:19.717 --> 00:15:23.155
You know, this week alone,
they canceled the Muppets.

00:15:23.155 --> 00:15:25.557
You know, they're canceling
Dr. Seuss.

00:15:25.557 --> 00:15:27.693
-First, they outlawed Dr. Seuss

00:15:27.693 --> 00:15:29.561
and now they want
to tell us what to say.

00:15:29.561 --> 00:15:31.529
-Ah, yes, the party
of the working class,

00:15:31.529 --> 00:15:33.432
if class in this case
means third grade.

00:15:33.432 --> 00:15:35.367
Do you guys really think
any actual adult

00:15:35.367 --> 00:15:37.603
in their right mind cares
about a few Dr. Seuss books

00:15:37.603 --> 00:15:39.972
getting pulled from publication
because of racist imagery?

00:15:39.972 --> 00:15:42.140
Even my kids don't care
about Dr. Seuss.

00:15:42.140 --> 00:15:44.242
They want to watch the League
of Legends World Championship,

00:15:44.242 --> 00:15:45.510
even though I'm still trying
to get them into

00:15:45.510 --> 00:15:47.412
my favorite board game,
"Ocean Master,"

00:15:47.412 --> 00:15:49.948
which has a new expansion
pack called "Port of Call."

00:15:49.948 --> 00:15:51.250
The way it works is

00:15:51.250 --> 00:15:52.751
you get skill cards
for every port you dock at,

00:15:52.751 --> 00:15:55.821
which helps you mine resources
which translate to gold coins,

00:15:55.821 --> 00:15:57.689
which you can then use
to hire deckhands

00:15:57.689 --> 00:16:00.325
who help you find islands
where you collect minerals,

00:16:00.325 --> 00:16:01.860
and whoever collects
the most minerals

00:16:01.860 --> 00:16:04.396
gets to pick
a different game to play.

00:16:04.396 --> 00:16:06.698
Republicans are preposterously
trying to rebrand themselves

00:16:06.698 --> 00:16:08.133
as a party of
working-class populists,

00:16:08.133 --> 00:16:10.435
despite the fact
that they're still in lockstep

00:16:10.435 --> 00:16:12.204
behind a racist
billionaire tax cheat

00:16:12.204 --> 00:16:14.272
who helped them dole out
trillions in tax cuts

00:16:14.272 --> 00:16:16.141
to corporations
and the wealthy.

00:16:16.141 --> 00:16:18.377
And now they're needlessly
putting workers in harms way

00:16:18.377 --> 00:16:21.280
by prematurely
lifting mask mandates.

00:16:21.280 --> 00:16:23.849
And one of them flew
to a luxury resort in Cancun

00:16:23.849 --> 00:16:25.517
while his constituents
froze to death.

00:16:25.517 --> 00:16:28.053
Meanwhile, courageous
Amazon workers in Alabama

00:16:28.053 --> 00:16:30.722
need and deserve the support,
and Republicans are silent.

00:16:30.722 --> 00:16:32.224
Turns out
there's only one worker

00:16:32.224 --> 00:16:33.725
they're willing to stand up for,
and that's...

00:16:33.725 --> 00:16:35.193
-Mr. Potato Head.

00:16:35.193 --> 00:16:37.195
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:16:37.195 --> 00:16:40.665
♪♪

00:16:40.665 --> 00:16:42.200
God's Love We Deliver
cooks and brings

00:16:42.200 --> 00:16:43.468
over two million meals a year

00:16:43.468 --> 00:16:45.504
to men, women and children
living with HIV AIDS,

00:16:45.504 --> 00:16:47.405
cancer, and other
serious illnesses,

00:16:47.405 --> 00:16:49.140
and they need your help
now more than ever.

00:16:49.140 --> 00:16:51.176
If you're watching this online,
you can hit the donate button.

00:16:51.176 --> 00:16:53.879
Stay safe,
wash your hands, wear a mask.

00:16:53.879 --> 00:16:54.747
We love you.

